  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) at 0.650 acc. Image-only with resnet50 is very weak (0.208 acc), raising the question of whether image features add any value when fused with a strong RNA signal. Uncertainty: We have no evidence on whether multimodal fusion improves or degrades performance relative to the best RNA-only setup. This experiment (config_031: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) tests whether adding image features to the known-best RNA configuration via weighted fusion provides complementary information. Weighted fusion is chosen over concat because it allows the model to down-weight the weak image signal (given the 0.208 image-only baseline), making this the safest multimodal test. It is the best use of the next budget slot because it answers the highest-level design question—whether the multimodal direction is worth pursuing at all—before committing further experiments to specific fusion or image-encoder variants. If it fails to beat 0.650, remaining budget can focus on RNA-only refinement; if it succeeds, a new promising direction opens."
}

